# Git on Windows is configured with core.autocrlf=true, and it guesses
# text vs binary by looking for a NUL byte near the start of the file.
# A reportlab PDF has none, so git classified docs/DIRECTOR-GUIDE.pdf as
# text and would have rewritten every LF to CRLF on checkout -- which
# corrupts the file. Images and woff2 fonts happen to carry an early NUL
# and were never at risk, but they are listed here so nobody has to
# rediscover why one of them is special.

* text=auto

*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff2 binary
